GTE MulMatrix family: recover Ghidra-dropped register/stack args (from dd2h.exe disasm)

The 3x3 fixed-point matrix multiply FUN_00413e08 @0x413e08 takes A in ESI, OUT in EDI
(both dropped by Ghidra -> unaff_ESI/EDI, bound to _g_esi/_g_edi globals), B in ECX (fastcall).
Its three wrappers load them as follows (dd2h.exe disasm):
- MulMatrix @0x4137c0 and gte_MulMatrix0 @0x4137ef are THREE-arg cdecl (m1,m2,out):
  esi=[ebp+8]=m1, ecx=[ebp+0xc]=m2, edi=[ebp+0x10]=out. Ghidra modeled only 2 args, silently
  DROPPING the out matrix everywhere -> the multiply wrote through an uninitialised _g_edi.
  All 10 binary call sites of gte_MulMatrix0 recovered from their push sequences (rightmost
  arg pushed first); each site's out annotated with its asm evidence inline.
- MulMatrix2 @0x41381e is (m1,m2) with out = scratch @0x4604a0 (mov edi,0x4604a0), then copies
  the scratch result into [ecx]=m2 (m2 = m1 x m2). Ghidra rendered that copy through
  extraout_ECX (a dropped ECX-after-call): ECX still holds param_2 because FUN_00413e08 never
  writes ecx (verified over 0x413e08..0x413f85) -> extraout_ECX = param_2.
This was the L8-10 crash (MulMatrix2 wild write via uninitialised _g_edi from Point_Camera) and
a geometry-correctness blocker everywhere else.
KNOWN REMAINING (next patches): callers building their matrices in Ghidra-scattered stack
shorts (Draw_Car, FUN_0042c2d4, FUN_00420708, Point_Camera local_3c..local_2c) need contiguous
buffers -- passing &sStack_NN relies on stack layout the compiler does not guarantee.

